window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>In <i>A Cacophony of Madness</i>, shadows rise, and destinies collide. Dahlia, a warrior driven by loss, stands at the brink of vengeance, seeking answers in a land where darkness reigns supreme. Across the sea, Draven, the son of a legendary captain, faces echoes of a vanished past as an ancient, cursed city reappears on the empire’s borders. But in the forsaken land of Sketan, where light fears to tread, Wrath prowls—a being draped in shadows and blood, bound to the sinister whispers of a crown that feeds on chaos.</p> <p>As these characters’ fates draw closer to Sketan’s haunted heart, The Wraith's influence seeps beyond its borders, threatening to unravel the very fabric of reality. Secrets long buried are revealed, loyalties are tested, and the line between hero and monster blurs. Can Dahlia and Draven survive the call of the abyss, or will they too fall to the madness that claims all who dare its depths?</p>"; 
